  "nl_text": "The rschema_0238 database is designed to manage information about classes, members, announcements, messages, logs, and applications within a community or organization. The database contains eight tables: class, member, announcement, message, log, application, member_message, and member_sent_message. The class table stores information about different classes, including their unique IDs, names, departments, and grades. Each member is represented in the member table, which includes their unique IDs, names, passwords, emails, ages, work units, phone numbers, and the class they belong to. The announcement table stores announcements made to specific classes, while the message table stores messages sent between members. The log table tracks the activities and moods of members, and the application table stores applications submitted by members. The member_message table links members with the messages they have sent or received, and the member_sent_message table tracks messages sent by one member to another. The database enforces referential integrity through foreign key constraints, which ensure that data in related tables is consistent and up-to-date, such as when a class is deleted, all related announcements and member information are also deleted.",
  "gold_question": "This is a Student Information Management System. The main functions of the system are as follows:\n1.Student Information Management: Manages basic student information such as student ID, name, gender, school, department, major, and ID number.\n2.Teacher Information Management: Manages teacher information, including teacher ID, name, gender, title, and contact number.\n3.Course Information Management: Manages course details, including course name, hours, credits, etc.\n4.Grade Management: Stores students’ performance data, including regular grades, experimental grades, mid-term grades, and final grades.\n5.Permission Management: Manages student and administrator permissions, including user ID, username, password, and role.\nEach teacher can teach multiple courses, and each course can be taught by multiple teachers.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0238.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0238\nCREATE TABLE `class` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `department` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `grade` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `member` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `age` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `work_unit` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(15) NOT NULL,\n  `class_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `member_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`class_id`) REFERENCES `class` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `announcement` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `class_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `announcement_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`class_id`) REFERENCES `class` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `message` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `sender_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `receiver_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `message_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`sender_id`) REFERENCES `member` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `message_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`receiver_id`) REFERENCES `member` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `log` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `member_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `activity` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `mood` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `log_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`member_id`) REFERENCES `member` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `application` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `member_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `application_content` text NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `application_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`member_id`) REFERENCES `member` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `member_message` (\n  `member_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `message_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`member_id`, `message_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `member_message_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`member_id`) REFERENCES `member` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `member_message_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`message_id`) REFERENCES `message` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `member_sent_message` (\n  `sender_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `receiver_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `message_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`sender_id`, `receiver_id`, `message_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `member_sent_message_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`sender_id`) REFERENCES `member` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `member_sent_message_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`receiver_id`) REFERENCES `member` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `member_sent_message_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`message_id`) REFERENCES `message` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
